/* ===== agent A a004: page-level datasources of PAGE_BOOSTERS / PAGE_NET_TREASURES =====
 * A page has its own source descriptor at page+0x48 (+0xc type 21 at page+0x54, +0x10 enum at +0x58, +0x14 at +0x5c,
 * +0x1c param at +0x64), dispatched by 0x763f40 like a widget's (item+0x24): enum +0x10, desc+0x14 -> event[0x24]
 * (PS3 event+120 = [0x1e]), desc+0x18 -> event[0x25], table param -> event[0x12], descriptor -> event+0x98.
 * PS3 1.19 menu.bin: PAGE_BOOSTERS page source = enum 0x44 (f_3466a8, the LIST_BOOSTERS source) with +0x14 = 0x89e96364;
 * PAGE_NET_TREASURES page source = enum 0xd9 (f_34d698, the LIST_TREASURE_SETS source) with +0x14 = 1. PS4 menu.bin keeps
 * them as enum 0x43 / 0xd4, both RET stubs (0x7597f0 / 0x759b90); their lists are already answered by boosters_source
 * (tag 0x4c414e43) and treasures_source (0x4c414ed4), so the page sources get the same tag (+0x14 stays, it is the
 * page-level marker those sources test). U3MP_PAGE_SOURCES=0 (ea[0] bit3) leaves them native. */
