/* ===== v5.45 Advanced Settings, stage 1: the 9 datasources of PS3 1.19 (absent from PS3 1.10 and PS4) =====
 * 1.19 adds BUTTON_CUSTOMRULES2 to PAGE_LOBBY (datasource 0x38 = 1.19 f_354ae4) and PAGE_CUSTOMRULES2 with 8 rows:
 * 0xe7 Respawn Time f_337ab0, 0xe8 Buddy Spawning f_337ca4, 0xe9 Health Multiplier f_337e78, 0xea Sprinting f_338064,
 * 0xec Weapon Mode f_33820c, 0xed Medal Kickbacks f_3383e4, 0xef Boosters f_3385b0, 0xee Grenade Rethrowing f_33877c.
 * PS4 has no datasource ids for them. The menu.bin patch (ASSETS) gives the widgets datasource 0xcf with the helper tag
 * 0x4c414f00|enum (0x4c414f38 for the button, 0x4c414fe7..0x4c414fef for the rows), so no runtime retag is needed.
 * The settings live in 1.19's custom-game block at NetGameManager +0x5544 (28 bytes, copied to clients). The new fields:
 * +0x5550 f32 respawn time, +0x5554 f32 health multiplier, +0x5558 u32 weapon mode, +0x555e bit1 buddy / bit0 sprint,
 * +0x555f bit7 kickbacks / bit6 rethrow / bit5 boosters. PS4's manager has no room for them, so they are kept in X.adv
 * with the same meaning. Defaults are set as in 1.19's net game select (f_31103c 0x311170 / 0x31128c): respawn = record
 * +0x20 (PS3 +32), health 1.0, weapon mode 0, all five toggles on. They are re-applied when the custom game selection
 * (0x17d167c) changes, which is where 1.19 runs that init. Stage 2 ports the game-side readers, stage 3 the client sync.
 * PS3 checks reproduced: *(0x17d5c58+0x3e4) != 2 (PS3 g+980) -> empty, value 0 (button, rows 0xe7/0xe9); title hidden for
 * game type 10 (respawn), 10/14 (buddy), 19 (kickbacks, boosters); op 8 "editable" = party leader (f_37f1f8: a LAN host
 * is its own leader); the button only for the leader and not in co-op (f_310c68 = type in {4,8,9,11,13,16,17,18}).
 * U3MP_ADV=0 (FUNCTIONS switch word bit0, rw2+0x3a70) answers none of them. Counters X.adv[7]: calls (low 16), sets (high 16). */
typedef struct { uint32_t sel1; uint32_t respawn,health,weapon; uint8_t f1,f2,pad[2]; uint32_t gt,count,stats; } AdvRules;   /* stats = X.adv[7] */
_Static_assert(sizeof(AdvRules)==32,"adv");
static AdvRules *adv(void){return (AdvRules*)X.adv;}
