/* ===== agent A a018: friends (PS3 1.19 NetFriends module 0x2ff08c..0x3017c0, friends datasources, quick actions) =====
 * PS4 kept the NetFriends object (PS3 0x1235900 = PS4 0x17caeb0, static init 0x71f8e8) and the UI that reads it (row click
 * 0x671f60 = f_29331c, players-met click 0x671580 = f_287e00, PLAYERSMET source 0x75e2e0 = f_351954), but dropped the module
 * that fills it (NP Basic friend list, presence, players history), the LIST_PSN_FRIENDS source (0xae, RET 0x76c4d0 =
 * f_350724), the PAGE_FRIENDACTIONS header (0x13, RET 0x75e150 = f_3491e4) and the own-presence publisher f_300538.
 * Ported here 1:1; every sceNp call goes through OnlineIfaceA v3 (ONLINE-IFACE-A.md section 4; offline stubs = not signed in).
 *
 * Object, PS3 -> PS4 (pointer growth; PS4 readers: count +0, entries +8, players met +0x10/+0x18, lock +0xc8; the static
 * init 0x71f8e8 clears exactly the qwords +0xc8 +0xd0 +0xe0 +0xf0 and the dword +0xc0 that this layout names):
 *  count +0, max +4, entries +8 (u32 -> u64); players met count +0xc -> +0x10, max +0x10 -> +0x14, entries +0x14 -> +0x18
 *  (0x28 each: NpId 0x24 + 4); "history changed" byte +0x18 -> +0x20; NpId +0x19 -> +0x21 (0x24); two 0x1b4 blocks +0x40/+0x44
 *  -> +0x48/+0x50; +0x48/+0x4c -> +0x58/+0x5c; last published presence data +0x50 -> +0x60 (0x60); next publish clock +0xb0
 *  -> +0xc0; list thread +0xb8 -> +0xc8 (the lock every reader tests); history thread +0xc0 -> +0xd0; add-history thread
 *  +0xd0 -> +0xe0; new-players max +0xd8 -> +0xe8, count +0xdc -> +0xec, names +0xe0 -> +0xf0 (0x10 x 0x24); Facebook
 *  thread +0xe8 -> +0xf8, id +0xf0 -> +0x100, NpId +0xf8 -> +0x108, name +0x11c -> +0x12c (the object ends at NGM 0x17cb060).
 * Entry 0x2f0 -> 0x240 (PS4 0x672075..0x6720a0 read size +0x1a8 (u64), data +0x128, state +0x1b0, NpId +1): flag +0; NpId
 *  +1 (PS4 keeps only the NpId of SceNpUserInfo: no online name, no avatar URL); presence details +0xdc -> +0x28: title
 *  +0, status +0x80, data +0x100, size +0x180 (u32 -> u64), state +0x184; Facebook id +0x268 -> +0x1b8, name +0x270 -> +0x1c0.
 * Presence state: PS4's in-context value is 1 (0x67208d tests state == 1 where 1.19 tests 2): FR_IN = 1 (PS3 2), FR_OUT = 2
 *  (PS3 1, out of context = another title; the community server never reports it), FR_OFF = 0. The sort keeps PS3's order
 *  (in > out > offline) through fr_rank.
 * Threads: PS3 runs the list / history / add-history fetches on PPU threads over the local NP Basic cache; here each runs to
 *  completion in the helper tick that starts it, its thread field set meanwhile, so readers see the same lock transitions.
 * Facebook (f_300300, f_300e74's FB part, the header avatar from graph.facebook.com, f_375bb0 "presence %s" on the social
 *  connection 0x136e6d0+0x130): not supported (user decision); f_93a5e0 (FB signed in) counts as 0, the FB fields stay 0.
 * Switch U3MP_FRIENDS119=0 (ea[1] bit5). Diagnostics ea[64..95] (see NOTES-a018). */
#define NFB(b) ((uint8_t*)((b)+0x17caeb0u))
#define FE_SZ 0x240u
#define FR_OFF 0
#define FR_IN 1
#define FR_OUT 2
/* v7.61 so02: f_3255b4(net) = net+0xc -> PS4 0x17d5c68. PS3 1.19 NetInit 0x297060..0x2970a0 sets it to DC net.bin 0x6f1c3f87 (0x64
 * in patch 18) OR the title's net-version family (u3h_key_family: retail, or beta / demo for the titles of f_449a8); PS4 never stores to it (0 from .bss), so the helper
 * keeps PS3's value there. fr_key_v: the beta form, taken over from a U3 friend's presence (RPCN thread). */
#define SO_NET_KEY (u3h_key_family(0) | 0x74u)   /* v7.66 rf01: the community game data's net.bin version (RPCS3 1.19 sends 0x74), retail family */
