/* ===== agent B b018: lobby stage logout at match start / cinema, PS3 1.19 f_30e43c mode 3 kept =====
 * PS3 1.19 NetGameManager setup f_31ef18 (PS4 0x72b570) ends with the stage loader f_30e43c(mgr, arg2 && !arg6, arg3, mode)
 * (0x320760..0x320788; PS4 0x72d2ef..0x72d30f: 0x743420(mgr, sil = arg2 & ~r9b, mode)). Mode 3 with the bool set is the
 * logout (PS3 0x30e998..0x30e9fc = PS4 0x7435ab..): find the current stage (name at mgr+24260 = PS4 +0x74b8), hide it
 * (f_8b55ec(l, 0) = 0x10f25b0(l, 0)) and unwant it (f_8bb9e4(mgr, name, 0) = removal from the want list +0x28). The name is
 * kept. The LAN custom match start is PS3 f_327dec 0x327f84..0x327fa4 = PS4 0x74bbb0 0x74bd09..0x74bd27: ShowPage
 * (PAGE_CUSTOM_LOAD 0x69e10dad), then f_31ef18(mgr, 1, 0, 3, 0, 0). The replay load Enter does the same (PS3 0x277314 =
 * PS4 0x66a358). The stage comes back only through the next f_30e43c call with mode 1/2 (0x30e75c: copy the netgame map
 * entry's stage name, want {flags 3}, show) or the bool-0 path (0x30ea00), e.g. PS3 f_327dec's lobby cases 0x327eb8/0x327f0c
 * (mode 1/2) = PS4 0x74be60/0x74bc1f. The clear f_8bd07c (PS3 0x31fa6c; PS4 0x10ee740 at 0x72bd93) drops only entries
 * without flag bit 1, so it never touches the stage ({flags 3}).
 * What went wrong on this build: the helper's stage_tick (LIST_PLAYERS op 6, every draw of a page that lists players) wants the
 * named stage again whenever its want entry is missing. Between the native logout and the match state (0x17d1868 == 2) it
 * re-wanted the stage, so the lobby stage stayed loaded and visible through the match (coop-syria-stage in Syria,
 * desert-multi-stage in Desert, A's capture), was put into the match world (Havok packfile marked in place, +0x28 = 0xff),
 * and after the match the world rebuild of Start Cinema (reset 0xc984e0 -> world init 0x11509d0 -> 0x1133bf0) could not
 * re-add the used packfile: fault at 0x122551. PS3 has no per-frame re-want: the stage is gone during the match and is
 * loaded fresh afterwards.
 * Port: stage_tick no longer undoes the logout. When the current stage's want entry disappears while its name is unchanged
 * (and stage_tick had it wanted on its previous call), that is f_30e43c mode 3: stage_tick then leaves the stage alone
 * (no want, no show, no lobby camera) until a native path wants it again (entry back) or names another stage. Fallback (not
 * PS3, no PS4 evidence yet that the post-match mode 1/2 call runs on the LAN flow): after a match (state 2 seen while held),
 * 300 stage_tick calls outside state 2 with the entry still missing let stage_tick want it again (a fresh load).
 * Switch: U3MP_STAGE_LOGOUT=0 (eb[0] bit5) = old behaviour. U3MP_STAGE_LOGOUT_FALLBACK=0 (eb[0] bit6) = no fallback.
 * Diagnostics: eb[174] logouts seen, eb[175] released by a new stage name, eb[176] released by a native re-want, eb[177]
 * released by the fallback, eb[178] stage_tick calls skipped while held, eb[179] held stage sid. */
