/* ===== agent E e003: lobby character switches to the hero / villain look when the player changes team (user item 3) =====
 * User decision: in the lobby the character takes the HERO or VILLAIN look as soon as the local player's team changes,
 * before Start Game, as PS3 1.19 does ONLINE. This is a deviation from PS3's LAN path, behind U3MP_LOBBY_SIDE_LIVE.
 * PS3 1.19 map:
 *  - placement f_24c05c (PS4 0x5b6640): online (net+60, PS4 net+0x40) it sets the custom manager's side from the local
 *    player's team, f_43a034(cm 0x127d6c0, f_367950(p)) (PS4 cm 0x17f9938, team 0x7927c0(p)), and takes that side's
 *    look; on LAN (net+60 == 0) it uses the side already in cm[0] (0x997a40: hero +0x620 / villain +0x648). The online net
 *    event 0x2f50c4 (PS4 0x6b17e9 / 0x6b1824) and the match setup 0x320c48 (PS4 0x73d4a7) make the same call. PS4 inlines
 *    f_43a034 (0x5b6826..0x5b686c): side <= 1 -> cm[0] = side; if the preview handle cm+0xf60 {ptr, id +0xf68} is live,
 *    0x995d50(cm) (= f_439eac, the preview refresh) and cm+0x104c = 1 (PS3 cm+3988). e03_43a034 is that inline.
 *  - f_43a174 (PS4 0x997230) keeps the packages of both sides wanted while the manager is active (loop over side 0 / 1),
 *    so the other side's look is resident and the new placement needs no load.
 *  - re-placement: the start of f_24c05c destroys a live character (f_249ec0 = 0x5b6c40); the MenuScene update f_24c52c
 *    (0x5b7240) places again in phase 2 whenever state is 2 and no character is live (0x24c82c = 0x5b77a8), with the
 *    entrance at menu-spawner-1. The exit is f_249cd0 (0x5b47c0, unless the exit anim 0xe4c14819 already plays), waited
 *    on through char+0x710 vt+0x60, exactly as the Start Game state 45 does (PS3 0x2bcff0 = PS4 0x6a7833).
 * Port (per NetUpdate frame, after k34_scene; only while the menu is up (f_267410), the scene is in state 2 / phase 2,
 * outside the match (0x17d1868 != 2) and outside the Start Game window (state machine 0x1b68810 in 0x2c..0x2e)):
 *  side = 0x7927c0(p) for p = NGM+0x370 (the f_367950 PS3's online placement uses). If side is 0 / 1 and differs from cm[0]:
 *  f_43a034(cm, side) (PS3's own call, in PS4's inline form); then, with a live character: exit (0x5b47c0, repeated each frame as
 *  state 45 does), wait until char+0x710 vt+0x60 reports the exit done (or 240 frames), destroy the character only
 *  (0x5b6c40; the scene stays in state 2 and keeps its props / camera), and the MenuScene's own phase-2 retry places the
 *  new look with its entrance. One exit and one entrance per change: no leave / enter of the scene, no second placement
 *  (the placement itself destroys any live character first). A team change while the character is exiting only
 *  updates cm[0]; the placement then takes the latest side. Leaving the scene (menu off, Start Game, match) cancels.
 * PS3's own online re-dress is in place: placement registers the lobby character as the custom manager's preview
 * (f_436170: cm+3756 = the character handle; PS4 cm+0xf60), so f_43a034's f_439eac (char vt+196 / f_959398 / vt+628)
 * swaps the live character's model and parts at once. As asked, the default here is the exit + entrance instead: in that
 * mode f_43a034 skips the in-place refresh when the preview is the lobby character (no pop before the exit); any other
 * live preview is refreshed as PS3 does. U3MP_LOBBY_SIDE_INPLACE=1 (eb[1] bit28, byte rw2+0x4057 bit4) gives PS3's
 * in-place re-dress instead (f_43a034 with the f_439eac refresh, no exit / entrance).
 * Switch U3MP_LOBBY_SIDE_LIVE=0 (eb[1] bit29, byte rw2+0x4057 bit5): PS3's LAN behaviour (look picked at placement only).
 * Diagnostics e03_d (EXT_BSS): [0] side changes applied (f_43a034 calls), [1] exits started, [2] characters re-placed
 * (destroyed after the exit), [3] exits ended by the 240-frame limit, [4] cancels (scene left during the exit),
 * [5] last {side | old cm[0] << 8 | team-function raw << 16}, [6] state (0 idle, 1 exiting), [7] exit frames. */
