/* ===== agent J j011: Co-op Weapon Mods page (user, v6.18): no guns in the weapon rows; mod toggles do not change the gun model =====
 * (a) Row gun image. PS3 1.19 f_341b2c (LIST co-op weapon) op 4 with slot 0 (0x341d54..0x341dbc) answers item type 33 with
 *     the co-op entry's weapon id: [2] = 33, [3] = 0, [4] = id, [5] = [6] = 0, [7] = -1, [8] = 0, [9] = -1, [10] = 1.0. The helper's
 *     port (coop_weapon_source) had no slot-0 case, so the rows had no image. PS4's own weapon list 0x766870 answers the same
 *     type 0x21 (0x7671d4..0x767209) in PS4's layout: [2] = 0x21, [4..5] = 0, [6] = id, [7] = [8] = 0, [9] = -1, [10] = 0,
 *     [11] = -1, [12] = 1.0. j11_rowimg writes that.
 * (b) Model refresh. PS3 1.10 f_33a3b8 (co-op mods list) op 22 (0x33a488..0x33a4b8): after the toggle, f_253bdc(preview,
 *     f_355c54(profile, weapon) = the weapon's mod mask, 255). PS4 inlines f_253bdc in its own mods list 0x7680f0 (0x768686..
 *     0x7686cc, 0x768a70..0x768acd): preview handle 0x17bba90+0x1490 / id +0x1498 (process = *handle when process+0x7c == id),
 *     process+0x6f0 (u16) = mask, +0x6f2 = the byte unless it is 255, then 0xd49270(process) rebuilds the gun with its mods.
 *     The helper's co-op mods port (coop_mods_source) had left this out. j11_preview does it after every toggle.
 * Switch U3MP_COOP_MODS119=0 (eb[2] bit2) leaves both out. j11_d: [0] row images, [1] previews refreshed, [2] refresh
 * without a live preview, [3] last mask. */
