/* ===== agent J j012: Fort white band / Museum blow-out, runtime side: live render-settings snapshot + opt-in experiments =====
 * Static findings (frame constants builder 0xf0ac40, live render settings 0x1b3b4e0, field names from the render-settings
 * dump 0x1211010):
 *  - general + floor fog (0xf0b500..0xf0b606): [0x20] = density rs+0x250 (only when multiplier rs+0x23c >= 1.0), floor fog
 *    [0x28] = min(density * floor-fog-density-multiplier rs+0x298, 1), floor start/range rs+0x274 / +0x278. Batch89d D1
 *    zeroed rs+0x250, which zeroes BOTH, and changed nothing: the white is not this fog.
 *  - sky fog (0xf0b60b..0xf0b6d4), a second fog block NOT touched by D1: colour rs+0x4a0..0x4a8 (raw, constant, no exposure
 *    term), multiplier rs+0x4ac (density used only when >= 1.0), distance start/range rs+0x4b0 / +0x4b4, HEIGHT start/range
 *    rs+0x4b8 / +0x4bc, density rs+0x4c0. A height-banded fog that D1 left on: the best candidate for "white beyond ~8 m
 *    within a height band".
 *  - exposure: tonemap block 0xedff80 hands the GPU the auto range [rs+0x6f4, rs+0x6f8] (method rs+0x6f0; +0x70 bit31 =
 *    CPU-chosen EV, used for method 0 and for method 1 with the override tm+0x218 / EV tm+0x214). a022 substitutes the
 *    CPU copy B (tm+0x210, used for particle tints w = 1/(2^filmic-bias * B) at 0xf0ae3d and the pickup shimmer) with
 *    2^((min+max)/2) because the port never fills the GPU readback. If the port's GPU auto-exposure lands elsewhere, the
 *    scene, fog colour and particles do not agree; constant-colour terms (fog colour) blow out first.
 * j012 adds (no behaviour change by default):
 *  - j12_d (24 words, refreshed every frame while MP is active): [0] frames, [1] tonemap method, [2] range min, [3] max,
 *    [4] manual EV, [5] curve type, [6] filmic bias, [7] use-improved, [8] improved bias, [9] B (tm+0x210), [10] tm+0x214,
 *    [11] tm+0x218 byte, [12] fog density rs+0x250, [13] fog multiplier rs+0x23c, [14] fog colour r, [15] floor-fog density
 *    multiplier, [16] sky-fog multiplier rs+0x4ac, [17] sky-fog density rs+0x4c0, [18] sky-fog height start, [19] height
 *    range, [20] sky-fog colour r, [21] sky-fog distance start, [22] distance range, [23] experiments applied (bits).
 *  - experiments, builder opt-in (eb[2] bits, all default OFF):
 *    U3MP_EXPO_LOCK=1 (bit4): method-1 levels get tm+0x218 = 1, tm+0x214 = (min+max)/2, so the GPU uses the CPU EV, the same
 *      value a022 gives B (scene, fog and particles then agree).
 *    U3MP_SKYFOG_OFF=1 (bit5): sky-fog multiplier rs+0x4ac = 0 (sky-fog density off).
 *    U3MP_FOG_ALL_OFF=1 (bit6): also the general fog multiplier rs+0x23c = 0.
 *    The render-settings writes go to the live block every frame (from the per-frame tick); j12_d[23] shows they ran. */
