/* ===== agent K k001 (4): Custom Game > Settings (PAGE_CUSTOMRULES 0x86799eee) drawn as PS3 1.19 =====
 * The page data is PS3's (batch42d menu.bin = 1.19 menu.bin: 9 rows, Score Limit, Round, Time Limit, Friendly Fire, Difficulty,
 * Global Chat, Power Plays, Treasure Chests, Weapon Pickups). Three PS4 differences broke it:
 * (a) Rows that do not apply to the game type (Round outside round modes, Difficulty outside co-op) stayed as blank rows. Their
 *     sources answer every op with "" (PS3 f_33727c / f_336c64 = PS4 0x754440 / 0x7546d0: rule step 0 -> text ""), so the label
 *     is empty. PS3 builds widget styles 6 and 13 with one class (page builder 0x2683ac, both cases -> ctor 0x210c7c) whose
 *     measure f_212e38 gives size 0 x 0 when the label is empty (f_24d4a8: op 1 text null or ""), whose focus test (vtable slot 7
 *     0x206d54) is the same label test and whose draw f_230194 draws nothing then. PS4's style-6 class (ctor 0x5e2590, vtable
 *     0x1678ef0) lost all three: measure 0x5df5f0 measures "" at full row height, focusable 0x622ee0 returns +0xad (1), draw
 *     0x5e2ae0 draws the empty row and its arrows (PS4's own label test 0x623010 survives only in another class, vt 0x1679100).
 *     Value stubs at the three entries (kinds 240 / 241 / 242), only for objects whose vtable is 0x1678ef0: no label -> not
 *     focusable, size 0 x 0, no draw (PS3's second measure test, op 7 > op 6, is not ported: PS4 answers those ops differently).
 * (b) Friendly Fire is style 13 in both menu.bins. PS3 builds 13 like 6 (same class); PS4 builds 13 as another control (ctor
 *     0x5ea8a0, used by its SP PAGE_GAMEPLAY_INGAME difficulty row) that puts the value far right. The row is set to style 6 at
 *     menu load (PAGE_CUSTOMRULES only), so it is PS3's class.
 * (c) Time Limit printed "minutes" without the number. PS3 f_337658 op 2 formats text 0x38e8ba93 / 0x9d59ec8a (1 minute) with
 *     the value (f_7ab93c); PS4 0x753e40 does the same with the PS4 texts, which carry no number (as Score Limit, fixed in
 *     time_limit_source). The row (id 0, enum 0x2a) is retagged 0xcf / 0x4c414e2a and k_time_source runs the native, then puts
 *     the value (rule +0x10 + step +0x18 * [1], PS4 0x753f29) in front when the text has no digit.
 * Switch U3MP_SETTINGS119=0 (byte rw2+0x4059 bit1; the builder also leaves the stubs out). k04_d: [0] rows hidden by the
 * focus test, [1] measures answered 0 x 0, [2] draws skipped, [3] Friendly Fire rows restyled, [4] Time Limit rows
 * retagged, [5] Time Limit texts given a number. */
