/* ===== fixer H h024: calibrated per-object auto-exposure EV (opt-in U3MP_EXPO_TABLE=1 = ec[1] bit18) =====
 * PS4 hands the GPU the auto range [rs+0x6f4, rs+0x6f8] (method rs+0x6f0 == 1); the GPU measures the scene and picks the EV.
 * PS3 1.19 does the same with its own RSX reduction. The port's GPU path picks EVs that disagree with PS3 per map (v6.55 EXPO A/B:
 * Village sunlit ground ~3x albedo and 9.5% R clipped at spawn, Oasis rocks clipped, Desert darker than PS3), and the GPU result
 * never reaches CPU memory, so the helper cannot measure luminance. h024 uses j012's override instead: for a method-1 object found
 * in h24_tab (match on live range min / max and filmic bias, +-0.01, so region blends at their end points still match) it sets
 * tm+0x218 = 1 and tm+0x214 = the calibrated EV clamped to the live range, every frame. Objects not in the table keep auto
 * exposure (London Streets 1.7 stops darker under the midpoint lock, Oasis brighter, Desert / Old Quarter match PS3 on auto). After a match is lost
 * the last EV is held for 120 frames (blend transitions), then the override is released (tm+0x218 = 0, unless j012's
 * U3MP_EXPO_LOCK is also on). The a022 shimmer-B stub follows tm+0x214 while tm+0x218 is set and this switch is on, so particle /
 * fog / pickup scales agree with the scene. Diagnostics ea[180..187]: [180] frames overridden, [181] frames released/no match,
 * [182] table index+1 in use (0 none), [183] EV written (float bits), [184] hold counter, [185] live min, [186] live max,
 * [187] live filmic bias. Peek h24=20ebf20:0x20. */
#pragma clang section text=".text.ext" rodata=".rodata.ext"
typedef struct { uint32_t mn,mx,fb,ev; } H24E;
static const H24E h24_tab[]={
 /* Sign: a HIGHER tm+0x214 EV is BRIGHTER (h024 calibration run baseline-1793343857262050500: Desert EV 1.7 was +0.84 / +1.17
  * stop over auto). */
 /* Village (village-multi 49cf00ad / a264dae0 / -01): midpoints. Auto sits above them (brighter end of the range): spawn -0.62
  * stop, sunlit ground 223,218,157 -> 174,165,94, 0% R>=250, sun/shadow 3.36x -> 4.59x linear. No PS3 reference; user judges. */
 {0x40180000u,0x409c0000u,0x3eccccabu,0x40680000u},{0x40000000u,0x408bd70au,0x3f000000u,0x404bd70au},
 {0x40600000u,0x40900000u,0xbf800000u,0x40800000u}};
 /* h024c: Desert Village removed: auto is within ~0.1 stop of PS3 (v632 matched views); matching auto would need EV 0.2..0.45, at
  * or below the range minimum 0.4. h024b: Oasis not in the table: the lock (EV 1.7, oasis.bin 6557a286 range 0.4..3.0) made it
  * BRIGHTER (shadowed cliff +1.17 stop linear), so Oasis auto sits below the midpoint, at or near the range MINIMUM 0.4 = the
  * darkest exposure PS3's range allows; the remaining clipping is not exposure. London Streets / Old Quarter stay on auto too. */
